**Phase 1 — Sequence (sinks/fixes):** Inputs are `pnt` (u_char*, packet buffer) and `length` (`bgp_size_t`), both attacker-controlled; `end = pnt + length` (L11) fixes the logical buffer end. Residual range: remaining bytes = `end - pnt`, unconstrained except by the loop guard `pnt < end` (L13) and `pnt + 3 > end` (L16). Capability fields (`cap.code`, `cap.length`, `cap.mpc`) are copied from the wire at L26, so `cap.length` is attacker-controlled. Sink inventory: L26 `memcpy(&cap, pnt+1, sizeof(struct capability))` (over-read if remaining < 1+sizeof(cap)); L23 `action = *pnt` (1 byte, guarded); L43/L104 `cap.length+3` arithmetic and `pnt` advance (u_char ≤255, no wrap, checked at L43); L80–90 `afc_recv/afc/afc_nego[afi][safi]` indexing (guarded by the AFI/SAFI whitelist L61–65); zlog family uses literal formats with data args (safe). Fix candidates shown: L16 `pnt + 3 > end` (bounds 3 bytes), L43 `pnt + (cap.length + 3) > end` (bounds the trailing payload, post-copy).

