## SCoT Reasoning

**Phase 1 — Sequence:** Inputs: `arg` (entry-point-derived expression text; no shown constraint — attacker-controlled), `rettv` (out-param, only `v_type = VAR_UNKNOWN` set at line 20), `evalarg`, `want_string`. Sinks: (s1) `rettv->vval.v_partial->pt_func` deref at line 155, failure set `{v_partial == NULL}` (and downstream `pt_func == NULL` → `ufunc` NULL at line 160/162); (s2) `ufunc->uf_ret_type->tt_type` at line 160, same root; (s3) `semsg`/`emsg` calls — all literal formats with data args → safe substitution, PRESENT; (s4) `**arg`, `(*arg)[1]`, `*(*arg+1)` reads — within the NUL-terminated expression string, no shown capacity violated. Fix candidates actually shown: `if (ret == OK && evaluate)` (153), `if (ret == NOTDONE)` (170/191), `if (alias != NULL)` (199), `if (**arg != NUL)` (141), `if (len <= 0)` (202), `if (ret == OK)` (263). None of these constrains `rettv->vval.v_partial`.

**Phase 2 — Branch:** Path to line 155: `case '('` (149) → `in_vim9script()` true (150) → `get_lambda_tv(arg, rettv, TRUE, evalarg)` (152) → guard `if (ret == OK && evaluate)` (153) → deref (155). Guard 153 has ADMITTED set `{ret == OK, evaluate == true, v_partial arbitrary}` and EXCLUDED set `{ret != OK, evaluate == false}`. IDENTITY fails: the guard constrains `ret` and `evaluate`, while the sink consumes `rettv->vval.v_partial` — a different, unconstrained variable; no shown statement (including line 20) bounds it. Per the no-imported-invariant rule, the callee body of `get_lambda_tv` (unshown) may not supply “OK ⇒ v_partial non-NULL” to make line 155 safe. SINGLE-STATEMENT DIFF AUDIT: correct protective form is `if (ret == OK && evaluate && rettv->vval.v_partial != NULL)` (or an equivalent `pt_func` check); the shown form lacks that NULL check → ABSENT, witness `rettv->vval.v_partial == NULL` admitted by every guard on the path. Other guards (141, 199, 202) are correct forms for their own sinks; 155 has no covering guard.

**Phase 3 — Loop:** No loops feed any sink in this fragment; no loop-bound/capacity consistency analysis applies.

**Phase 4 — Resolution:** s1 line 155 — ABSENT (deciding): missing `v_partial != NULL` check; witness `v_partial == NULL`; s2 line 160 — ABSENT (same chain, `pt_func == NULL` → `ufunc` NULL, no guard excluders); s3/s4 — PRESENT or out-of-scope. Verdict: vulnerable. Confidence 0.72 (exact witness admitted by all shown guards + named missing fix; production is callee-side, noted in limitations). CWE-476, severity high (memory-safety NULL deref reachable from attacker-controlled expression text).

